[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Sass Architecture and Variable Overrides in Bootstrap"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Bootstrap 5 is built natively on Sass, allowing developers to deeply customize the framework's design system without rewriting core stylesheets. Understanding Bootstrap's Sass architecture and the correct way to override default variables is crucial for maintaining a clean and scalable codebase."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding Bootstrap's Sass Architecture"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Bootstrap organizes its source files into distinct directories and partials. When setting up your custom build, you should structure your project to import Bootstrap correctly while inserting your custom variables and maps before the core framework compiles."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"_variables.scss: Contains all default global variables, color palettes, and spacing scales."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"_maps.scss: Contains Sass maps that assemble variables into logical groups for loops and utilities."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"_mixins.scss: Essential reusable logic for media queries, Flexbox helpers, and component styling."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"The Golden Rule of Variable Overrides"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"To successfully override a Bootstrap variable, your custom Sass file must define the variable with the !default flag or place it before Bootstrap's variables are loaded. Because Bootstrap's variables use the !default flag, any variable declared before importing Bootstrap will take precedence."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"// custom.scss

// 1. Include functions first
@import "../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/functions";

// 2. Override default variable values
$primary: #0d6efd;
$enable-shadows: true;
$prefix: "custom-";

// 3. Include rest of Bootstrap
@import "../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/variables";
@import "../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/maps";
@import "../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/mixins";
@import "../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/root";
@import "../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/utilities";
// Import remaining components..."},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Modifying Sass Maps"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"Many of Bootstrap's modern features rely on Sass maps rather than standalone variables. To add new colors or breakpoints, or to remove existing ones, you must use Sass map functions like map-merge or map-remove."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"@import "../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/functions";

// Add a custom color to the theme colors map
$custom-colors: (
  "brand": #ff5722
);

$theme-colors: map-merge($theme-colors, $custom-colors);

@import "../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/variables";
@import "../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/maps";
@import "../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/mixins";
@import "../node_modules/bootstrap/scss/bootstrap";"},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"By following this architecture, you ensure your project remains compatible with future Bootstrap updates while maintaining a completely bespoke design system. Always remember to load functions and variable overrides prior to compiling the core Bootstrap package."}]
